    {
      "id": "vscode",
      "title": "VS Code / VSCodium",
      "extension": "json",
      "description": "A local extension with all ten Solai themes, restrained syntax, workbench colours and the approved 16-colour integrated terminal palette.",
      "installation": [
        "Download the VSIX. In VS Code or VSCodium, run Extensions: Install from VSIX… from the Command Palette and choose solai-vscode.vsix. This is a local package, not a Marketplace installation.",
        "Run Preferences: Color Theme and choose Solai followed by a flavour and Light or Dark. Installing the extension does not select a theme, install fonts or change your editor settings.",
        "The individual JSON is theme source, not a settings.json replacement. To package it yourself, reference it from contributes.themes in an extension manifest; use uiTheme vs-dark for Dark or vs for Light.",
        "Semantic token rules apply when semantic highlighting is allowed by your settings. Bracket-pair colours apply only when your editor has bracket-pair colourization enabled. Language extensions and personal colour customizations can override theme colours.",
        "Integrated terminal ANSI indices are preserved exactly, including pale white slots in Light themes. VS Code may adjust rendered terminal contrast according to your existing minimum-contrast setting; applications may emit their own true colours."
      ],
      "variants": [
        {
